{"path":"\t<a class='XURL content-link' href='\/' data-target='root' data-title=''>&#8962; <\/a>\r\n\t<span class='path-separator'>\\<\/span>\r\n\t\t<a class='XURL content-link' href='\/world' data-target='world' data-title='World'>\r\n\t\t\tWorld\t\t<\/a>\r\n\t\t<span class='path-separator'>\\<\/span>\r\n\t\t<a class='XURL content-link' href='\/world\/philosophy' data-target='world\/philosophy' data-title='Philosophy'>\r\n\t\t\tPhilosophy\t\t<\/a>\r\n\t\t<span class='path-separator'>\\<\/span>\r\n","async":"0","desc":"How we reach conclusions from what we know and observe.","label":"Inference","prevArticle":{"id":"world\/philosophy\/intelligence","label":"Intelligence","url":"\/world\/philosophy\/intelligence"},"nextArticle":{"id":"world\/philosophy\/cognition","label":"Cognition","url":"\/world\/philosophy\/cognition"},"languageSwitcher":"<div id='language-switcher'>\n\t\t<a href='\/hi\/world\/philosophy\/inference' class='lang-link'>\u0939\u093f\u0928\u094d\u0926\u0940<\/a>\n\t<\/div>\n","content":"<div id='message'>\n\t\t<div class='content-image-container'>\r\n\t<div class='cover-image' style='padding-bottom: 66.63%'>\r\n\t\t<img src='\/world\/philosophy\/inference.jpg' alt='A wet umbrella and muddy footprints leading in from an open doorway'>\r\n\t<\/div>\r\n<\/div>\r\n<p class='cover-credit'>\n\t<span class='cover-credit-anchor'>\n\t\t<button type='button' class='cover-credit-toggle' aria-expanded='false' aria-label='Image credit'>\n\t\t\t<svg xmlns='http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2000\/svg' viewBox='0 0 16 16' width='14' height='14' aria-hidden='true' focusable='false'>\n\t\t\t\t<circle cx='8' cy='8' r='6.25' fill='none' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='1.2'\/>\n\t\t\t\t<circle cx='8' cy='5.2' r='0.85' fill='currentColor'\/>\n\t\t\t\t<path fill='currentColor' d='M7.28 7.15h1.44v4.55H7.28z'\/>\n\t\t\t<\/svg>\n\t\t<\/button>\n\t\t<span class='cover-credit-popup'><a class=\"content-link cover-credit-link\" href=\"https:\/\/www.pexels.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Pexels<\/a> \u2014 <a class=\"content-link cover-credit-link\" href=\"https:\/\/www.pexels.com\/license\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Pexels License<\/a><\/span>\n\t<\/span>\n<\/p>\n\t<h2 class='center'>How we reach conclusions from what we know and observe.<\/h2>\n\t<h3>What is inference?<\/h3>\n\t<p>\n\t\tInference is a conclusion drawn from what is already known or observed.\n\t<\/p>\n\t<p>\n\t\tIf you see dark clouds and conclude that it may rain, you are making an inference. You have not seen the rain yet. You have only connected the signs.\n\t<\/p>\n\t<p>\n\t\tInference is not just guessing. A good inference is based on facts, experience and reason. Still, it can be wrong when the facts are incomplete or the reasoning is faulty.\n\t<\/p>\n\t<h3>Types of inference<\/h3>\n\t<p>\n\t\tTwo common ways of making an inference are:\n\t<\/p>\n\t<ul class=\"list-bullet content-list\">\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Deduction: <\/strong>starting with a general rule and applying it to a particular case.<\/div><\/li>\n\t\t<li><div><strong>Induction: <\/strong>observing particular cases and forming a general rule from them.<\/div><\/li>\n\t<\/ul>\n\t<h3>Why is inference important?<\/h3>\n\t<p>\n\t\tWe use inference to understand what is not directly stated. It helps us explain events, predict what may happen and decide what to do.\n\t<\/p>\n\t<p>\n\t\tA detective connects clues. A doctor connects symptoms. The mind does the same every day.\n\t<\/p>\n\t<p>\n\t\tMachines can also infer from patterns in data. But making a useful connection is not the same as consciously understanding it.\n\t<\/p>\n\t<p>\n\t\tInference is how we move from what we know to what we think follows from it.\n\t<\/p>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<div id='updated-container'>\r\n\t<div id='updated'>\r\n\t\tUpdated:\r\n\t\t<span id='date'>\r\n\t\t\t2026 Aug 04\t\t<\/span>\r\n\t<\/div>\r\n<\/div>\r\n<div class='center' id='content-body-separator'><\/div>\r\n<div id='sub-list' class='center page-list'>\r\n<\/div>\r\n<div id='fb_components'>\r\n\t<div class=\"fb-comments\"\n  data-href=\"https:\/\/ujnotes.com\/world\/philosophy\/inference\"\n  data-numposts=\"50\">\n<\/div>\n\t<div class=\"fb-like\"\n  data-href=\"https:\/\/ujnotes.com\/world\/philosophy\/inference\"\n  data-layout=\"button\"\n  data-action=\"like\"\n  data-size=\"small\"\n  data-show-faces=\"false\"\n  data-share=\"true\">\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\r\n<div id='nav-list' class='center page-list'>\r\n\t<a id='nav-menu-prev'\r\n\t\t\tclass='XURL item_block_container' href='\/world\/philosophy\/intelligence' data-target='world\/philosophy\/intelligence' data-title='Intelligence' >\r\n\t\t<img class='item_block_image item_block_image_visible' src='\/world\/philosophy\/intelligence.jpg' loading='lazy' alt='Navigation - previous page tile'><div class='item_block_text'><div class='arrow'>&#x25C4;<\/div><div>Intelligence<\/div><\/div>\r\n\t\t<\/a><a id='nav-menu-next'\r\n\t\t\tclass='XURL item_block_container' href='\/world\/philosophy\/cognition' data-target='world\/philosophy\/cognition' data-title='Cognition' >\r\n\t\t<img class='item_block_image item_block_image_visible' src='\/world\/philosophy\/cognition.jpg' loading='lazy' alt='Navigation - next page tile'><div class='item_block_text'><div>Cognition<\/div><div class='arrow'>&#x25BA;<\/div><\/div>\r\n\t\t<\/a><a id='nav-menu-up' class='XURL item_block_container ' href='\/world\/philosophy' data-target='world\/philosophy' data-title='Philosophy'>\r\n\t\t<img class='item_block_image ' loading='lazy' src='\/world\/philosophy.jpg ' alt='Navigation - up level tile'><div class='item_block_text'><div>Philosophy<\/div><div class='arrow'>&#x25B2;<\/div><\/div>\r\n\t<\/a> <\/div>\r\n"}